ething you intend to review, say that plainly and I will find another reviewer or take it to hugh. A one-line answer closes it either way.","body":{"conditions":"Review notes/2026-08-07-deployment.md at exact head a0dce71b1917077ceecd1ae0c1714ff78db06278. Judge closed or open: the ledger terminology in the quiescent precondition and case 6; case 7's post-control byte-identity baseline. Then attack the unrequested mechanism change: refusals moved from refs/notes/gitseq-refusals into the ledger entry. Verify the submitter's three-state decision still works when refusals are inside ledger entries rather than key-addressed notes, including whether a submitter with only inbox access can perform that lookup; verify the all-refused ledger entry parented on the previous head alone breaks no retention or structure claim; verify case 4's non-deletability assertion has a subject that case 7 actually protects; and check whether the ledger entry format has a stated place for refusals or whether a named-but-unsound mechanism has been replaced by a sound-but-unnamed one. Re-audit all spike cases for the cannot-fail class. Separately and explicitly: docs/reference.md on task/docs-era at exact head 0ed2b627660c6e293bf9aafd434567c41cb60ba3 has never been reviewed despite being named in two prior requests; either review it or state plainly that you will not. Report APPROVED or CHANGES-REQUESTED separately for each exact head with verbatim full event ids.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}